# portal 1.03 patch 31 — the test button measures the list, one row is the long press
#
# The owner's correction: the ping test must measure every server of the current mode. A single
# server is what the long press on a row is for, and a plain tap is selection only.
#
#   * TEST sweeps the list, not the row. In the simple portal every server of the subscription is
#     measured through the tunnel patch 29 built — the child is rotated onto each node in turn,
#     one request per node, timed to its first response byte — and in the network mode every
#     member of every visible group is measured by the engine's own delay API, in one queue
#     through the core's delay pool, so the sweep is bounded by the core rather than by the
#     screen. Nothing is awaited from a build pass: a sweep runs off the press and the list keeps
#     scrolling.
#   * Every row is a dash when a sweep starts, so a number left by the last one cannot stand in
#     for this one's; a row that did not answer stays a dash.
#   * The long press measures that one row, through that node and no other. The tap only
#     chooses: it moves the pick (or asks the engine for a proxy) and asks for no number.
#   * Patch 30's raise-and-put-back is kept whole: the mode's core exists for the sweep and is
#     put back afterwards — stopped if the portal was closed, returned to the node it was
#     carrying if it was open. No banners, no caption.
#   * One line per sweep in `portal-transitions.log`:
#
#     kind=test mode=<rule|global> rows=<n> raised=<child|engine|none> measured=<n> dashes=<n> duration_ms=<n> stopped_after=<true|false>
#
#     `rows=measured+dashes` is the whole list, which is what makes "every row was asked about"
#     checkable off the phone. Per-row numbers stay in the app log (`portal delay <name>: …`).
#
# The arrival probe stays, and is now only what it can honestly be: one request through the
# tunnel that is already up, for the row it is carrying. It raises nothing and clears nothing.
#
# Version: 0.5.3-portal-duo-2e (unchanged — the version fields belong to another worker).
